# Process attention — hero event tags

Reuse the queue symbols from [next-items.md](../plans/next-items.md). **One inline tag per named hero / work block** — not on daily consumption, scare-only lines, or hazard audit rows.

## Symbols

| Tag | Meaning | Examples |
|---|---|---|
| **⚒** | **Hands-on** — attention for the whole block | Weaving · haul laps · forge · measure pass · farm hero |
| **⧗** | **Clock** — start and walk away | Submerged block cure · rett in ditch · ferment · drying |
| **⚒→⧗** | **Load then clock** — setup, then elapsed time | Retort · kiln load · lime slake · cheese set |

Add **duration only when it helps**: `~½ h` · `~half-day` · `full day` · `~6 h burn` · `90 d cure`. For **⚒→⧗**, name the **return beat** when non-obvious (`unload eve` · `pull ~d####`).

## Placement

On the **event header** line, after grammar refs:

```markdown
### ✓ **`CHAR-RETORT-4293` @ pit lane** *(⚒→⧗ · ~6 h · unload eve · d4193 grammar)*
### ✓ **`WW-2-Q-SPRING-SERIES-PT3` @ S2-0`** *(⚒ ~½ h)*
### ✓ **`WOOD-HAUL-4291` @ T-1 margin** *(⚒ full day · d4192 grammar)*
```

Split days: tag **each** block (`AM` wood **⚒** · `PM` sand **⚒**). A quick pass bundled with a hero day gets its **own** tag — do not inflate the hero to full day.

## Do not

- Tag passive inventory clocks already tracked in `now.md` unless today's file **opens or closes** that clock.
- Use **⧗** for work that still needs a human watching (forge heat, smelt tending) — that is **⚒**.
- Invent precise minutes; band classes are enough (`~½ h` · `~half-day` · `full day`).
